  "id": "substitution-hypothesis",
  "term": "substitution hypothesis",
  "definition": "In this context, the substitution hypothesis is the idea that time spent watching television displaces other beneficial activities, such as leisure reading or interacting with a parent. It predicts that more TV viewing earlier will be linked to less of those activities later, which could help explain poorer reading achievement.",
